WEBVTT

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:34.510
Flowing Away

00:01:34.510 --> 00:01:38.510
SHOGI HALL

00:01:41.510 --> 00:01:43.520
Meijin Touji Souya
The Challenge
to a Beautiful Future

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:45.520
The 43rd Newcomer Tournament
Commemorative Match
2008 Newcomer King, Rei Kiriyama 5th-Dan

00:01:53.570 --> 00:01:57.030
What is this? What is this poster?

00:01:57.030 --> 00:02:00.160
What is this? Why is the design so cool?

00:02:00.530 --> 00:02:05.580
It's on really nice paper, and it looks like
the letters are popping off the page.

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:09.170
It's just a commemorative battle between
the Newcomer King and a Meijin, right?

00:02:09.460 --> 00:02:14.460
Parts of it have like a matte finish
and other parts of it are shiny...

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:16.420
A special manufacturing process?

00:02:16.420 --> 00:02:20.180
What is this? Why are they making
incredible posters like these?

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:20.970
JAB

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:22.430
Yo! Did you notice?

00:02:22.430 --> 00:02:24.020
Cool, right?

00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:25.890
You guys have some expert eyes.

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:29.810
I hired a designer to do it!
I told him to make it cool.

00:02:29.810 --> 00:02:31.860
I even splurged on the printing.

00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:34.230
I don't want to hear it, Toku!

00:02:34.570 --> 00:02:37.030
I mean, our posters look like that!

00:02:37.030 --> 00:02:39.660
33rd Kishou Championship

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:39.660
Only necessary
information included

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:39.660
PLAIN...

00:02:39.990 --> 00:02:43.330
When was that photo taken?
What occasion was it originally used for?

00:02:43.330 --> 00:02:45.540
The picture is kind of grainy!

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:46.790
Tell me!

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:46.790
NERVOUS
NERVOUS

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:50.000
And... how can I put this?

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:55.590
This poster wasn't professionally printed,
but made by the Association, wasn't it?

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:55.590
NERVOUS
NERVOUS

00:02:55.760 --> 00:02:59.930
And not only that, how should I say this,
the photo of the hotel venue is strangely,

00:03:00.050 --> 00:03:02.680
no, definitely way bigger than we are!

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:06.180
EEEEK

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:06.640
That's awful!

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:10.560
How can you treat us like this just because
Kiriyama and Souya are a bit younger and cuter?

00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:13.310
My eternal Kishou Championship title
is on the line!

00:03:12.230 --> 00:03:13.310
ETERNAL

00:03:13.310 --> 00:03:16.860
Not to mention, that poster is kind of small!

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:19.780
What do you want me to do?

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:23.620
We're in a recession and barely scraping by
because of lack of sponsors!

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:25.740
And besides, what was that first match?

00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:29.750
Fans won't come, and the players'
match is as shaky as their broken-down bodies!

00:03:32.290 --> 00:03:33.540
Can't say anything back...

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:36.550
VIDEO REPLAY

00:03:39.550 --> 00:03:46.560
Old man, one step away from pneumonia

00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:56.070
Chronic gastritis (about to become a stomach ulcer)

00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:56.070
CREAK
CREAK

00:04:04.910 --> 00:04:08.410
CREAK
CREAK
CREAK

00:04:04.910 --> 00:04:08.410
COUGH
GLOUGH
COUGH

00:04:08.410 --> 00:04:13.670
The Sickly Showdown

00:04:09.870 --> 00:04:13.670
What was that game between two invalids?
Your bodies are too weak!

00:04:14.290 --> 00:04:17.460
On top of that, it was
an unsightly psychological battle.

00:04:20.380 --> 00:04:23.430
Sh-Shimada, is the head of your King
looking a bit thin?

00:04:23.430 --> 00:04:27.060
Your King. It isn't getting a bit thin on top?

00:04:28.970 --> 00:04:33.230
CREAK
CREAK
CREAK

00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:31.230
It is not thin.

00:04:31.230 --> 00:04:33.230
That's how I like it.

00:04:33.230 --> 00:04:35.230
What was that? What kind of battle?!

00:04:35.560 --> 00:04:37.730
Full of coughing and grinding teeth
and abusive language!

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:40.940
In recent years,
playing quietly was the norm!

00:04:40.940 --> 00:04:44.860
When is your shogi from?
The Showa period? Are you guys from the 80s?!

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:52.120
WHISPER

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:51.750
People watching them live
on the net were having a blast, though.

00:04:52.120 --> 00:04:53.210
Demo Board Commentator

00:04:53.210 --> 00:04:56.630
VIDEO REPLAY

00:04:53.580 --> 00:04:59.630
It was an "at-home" feel with not many people,
so that actually made it really exciting.

00:05:00.050 --> 00:05:03.880
Whoa! Shimada 8th-Dan
moves his Silver to 5-1 left.

00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:04.260
ON THE NET

00:05:04.260 --> 00:05:09.390
Kishou Championship Second Match

00:05:04.930 --> 00:05:07.640
Huh? Silver to 5-1 left?

00:05:09.890 --> 00:05:10.640
DOUBLE TAKE

00:05:11.270 --> 00:05:15.600
Silver to 5-1 left? Why would he do that?

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:19.270
Just between you and me, I have a feeling
that's going to cost him the game.

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:22.150
Seriously? Silver to 5-1 left?

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:26.530
There are so few
people in the demo
board room
that everyone's
sitting in a circle...

00:05:22.490 --> 00:05:24.400
Oh yeah! That's no good!

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:26.530
That is a lousy move, isn't it?

00:05:26.780 --> 00:05:27.820
Ugh!

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:31.790
If you don't like it, then get your health back
and some sponsors, too!

00:05:31.790 --> 00:05:36.210
Support:
Morisen Publishing
Morioka Bookstore
Hanamaki Electronics
Etc.

00:05:31.790 --> 00:05:36.210
BA-BAM

00:05:32.290 --> 00:05:36.210
Look at this! See how popular
Souya and Kiriyama are?

00:05:36.330 --> 00:05:39.040
Damn it, Shimada! It's your fault!

00:05:40.710 --> 00:05:44.670
If Gakuto were the challenger,
this place would be packed with female fans!

00:05:47.220 --> 00:05:48.430
I'll be waiting for you.

00:05:48.430 --> 00:05:51.430
Kishou Championship Spectator Bus Tour,
including a lunch party with both players

00:05:51.770 --> 00:05:53.680
It's my fault? What?

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:56.690
SHOGI HALL

00:05:58.440 --> 00:06:04.690
True, we both have lousy health
and that game was somewhat appalling,

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:07.950
but however you get there, a win is a win.

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:09.700
And I won!

00:06:09.950 --> 00:06:11.580
Not only that...

00:06:11.910 --> 00:06:14.870
I'm going to win the next one too.

00:06:14.870 --> 00:06:18.080
I won't let anyone
take the Kishou title away from me.

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:19.830
It's my life!

00:06:21.250 --> 00:06:22.960
Mr. Yanagihara.

00:06:23.670 --> 00:06:28.010
Souya is putting everything into the Meijin Battle,
so the other tournaments become empty.

00:06:28.010 --> 00:06:31.640
This is the one title I'm hanging on to,
even if it kills me!

00:06:31.640 --> 00:06:33.470
Farewell, gentlemen!

00:06:37.810 --> 00:06:40.190
You didn't have to be that blunt!

00:06:40.190 --> 00:06:44.190
Go home, get a good night's sleep,
and let your body rest!

00:06:44.190 --> 00:06:46.360
I wasted my time thinking you were cool!

00:06:52.120 --> 00:06:55.750
Well, you two can keep going at it like that.

00:06:55.750 --> 00:07:02.000
SOUYA AND
KIRIYAMA POSTERS

00:06:56.200 --> 00:07:02.000
I'm going to get people psyched for this
high-profile match, Souya versus Kiriyama.

00:07:03.750 --> 00:07:06.760
HAHAHA!

00:07:12.180 --> 00:07:13.600
But Chairman,

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:16.930
please go easy on them.

00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:23.230
I think neither Souya nor Kiriyama
are comfortable being the center of attention.

00:07:24.520 --> 00:07:29.740
I know. I've known Souya for a long time too.
So I know that about him.

00:07:30.490 --> 00:07:34.530
I'm not going to kill the golden goose.

00:07:44.040 --> 00:07:46.840
I see. Kiriyama...

00:07:48.760 --> 00:07:50.880
So you're facing Souya...

00:07:51.680 --> 00:07:53.300
at last.

00:08:08.820 --> 00:08:11.610
Hey, Kiriyama. There you are.

00:08:20.290 --> 00:08:22.420
<i>Incredible concentration.</i>

00:08:23.170 --> 00:08:25.040
<i>He can't even hear me.</i>

00:08:28.670 --> 00:08:29.960
The precious game record!

00:08:32.470 --> 00:08:34.430
Hey, Kiriyama.

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:36.430
Oh, Mr. Hayashida.

00:08:37.010 --> 00:08:40.640
That commemorative match
is in Morioka, right? Are you ready for it?

00:08:40.640 --> 00:08:43.730
Yes. There's really nothing to prepare for.

00:08:43.730 --> 00:08:45.270
Are you going to wear a kimono?

00:08:45.270 --> 00:08:48.320
No, the chairman said
my school uniform was okay.

00:08:50.530 --> 00:08:51.320
Are you nervous?

00:08:53.910 --> 00:08:54.860
Yes.

00:08:56.910 --> 00:08:59.870
But for some reason,
it doesn't feel real to me.

00:09:02.040 --> 00:09:03.580
Oh, that's right! Mr. Hayashida...

00:09:08.130 --> 00:09:09.500
I see.

00:09:10.420 --> 00:09:11.970
So it's been resolved.

00:09:12.920 --> 00:09:13.720
Yes.

00:09:15.300 --> 00:09:19.720
It's like the air around her is totally different.

00:09:23.440 --> 00:09:26.980
Kind of like a light, airy feeling.

00:09:28.060 --> 00:09:30.980
She said there's nothing
to worry about anymore.

00:09:32.360 --> 00:09:37.030
She's let all of her muscles relax
and can just rest easy.

00:09:39.450 --> 00:09:44.370
It makes me think about
just how much she suffered all that time.

00:09:50.710 --> 00:09:52.510
That's great, Kiriyama.

00:09:53.840 --> 00:09:58.010
No, Mr. Hayashida, I...

00:09:59.100 --> 00:10:03.020
In the end, I wasn't any help at all.

00:10:04.520 --> 00:10:06.900
Did you tell her that?

00:10:09.400 --> 00:10:10.400
Yes.

00:10:12.030 --> 00:10:14.780
And what did she say?

00:10:14.780 --> 00:10:17.410
What? Um...

00:10:20.530 --> 00:10:23.410
She said, "That's not true," didn't she?

00:10:28.580 --> 00:10:29.710
Yes.

00:10:31.340 --> 00:10:33.710
What, but, how did you know?

00:10:33.710 --> 00:10:35.970
It's easy to figure out.

00:10:35.970 --> 00:10:38.050
I've been listening to you this whole time.

00:10:38.930 --> 00:10:42.180
So I know you were doing
everything you could to help her

00:10:42.180 --> 00:10:47.600
and that she's a girl with a good head on her
shoulders who understands all kinds of things.

00:10:48.980 --> 00:10:50.860
Results are important,

00:10:51.060 --> 00:10:55.570
but it's not results that reach people, Kiriyama.

00:10:56.700 --> 00:11:00.320
The world doesn't revolve around results.

00:11:04.910 --> 00:11:07.580
Good luck with the commemorative match.

00:11:09.620 --> 00:11:10.750
Thank you.

00:11:17.260 --> 00:11:22.930
<i>I had to attend a party on the eve of the match,
so I met up with people from newspapers</i>

00:11:23.180 --> 00:11:25.890
<i>and the Association that afternoon.</i>

00:11:32.190 --> 00:11:34.190
<i>We took a bullet train there.</i>

00:11:37.820 --> 00:11:42.120
<i>Meijin Souya was sitting
some seats away from me.</i>

00:11:43.870 --> 00:11:46.160
<i>His profile face with his eyes closed.</i>

00:11:47.160 --> 00:11:49.120
<i>No sound came from that profile,</i>

00:11:50.580 --> 00:11:53.670
<i>just like the bottom of a lake.</i>

00:12:07.390 --> 00:12:09.980
<i>Stillness and a violent storm...</i>

00:12:11.730 --> 00:12:18.070
<i>That was the beginning of four days
I never could have imagined.</i>

00:12:18.990 --> 00:12:20.990
Flowing Away

00:12:20.990 --> 00:12:24.990
White Storm (Part 1)

00:12:45.930 --> 00:12:51.980
<i>I-It's a much bigger hotel than I had pictured.</i>

00:12:52.520 --> 00:12:54.770
Welcome
Newcomer Tournament Commemorative Match
Meijin Touji Souya and Rei Kiriyama 5th-Dan

00:12:54.770 --> 00:12:57.270
LINED UP

00:12:57.610 --> 00:12:59.860
Welcome!

00:12:59.860 --> 00:13:03.030
Hi! Thanks. I appreciate the hospitality.

00:13:03.700 --> 00:13:07.530
We've been waiting for you.
Here, let me take your bag.

00:13:08.870 --> 00:13:13.500
Great. This is one of the stars of the show,
Kiriyama 5th-Dan.

00:13:13.670 --> 00:13:14.790
Take care of him!

00:13:14.790 --> 00:13:17.790
BA-BAAM

00:13:18.550 --> 00:13:23.550
Well then, why don't we go to our rooms first?

00:13:33.310 --> 00:13:35.020
What is this?

00:13:36.560 --> 00:13:39.570
GOSHO LAKE

00:13:39.980 --> 00:13:42.320
This is your room, Kiriyama.

00:13:42.320 --> 00:13:44.820
SPACIOUS

00:13:45.070 --> 00:13:46.950
Isn't the Gosho Lake pretty?

00:13:47.070 --> 00:13:47.410
SLAP

00:13:47.070 --> 00:13:50.410
Well, you've got free time
until the reception at 7:00.

00:13:50.700 --> 00:13:51.950
So relax!

00:13:52.000 --> 00:13:53.080
SHOVE

00:13:53.160 --> 00:13:54.040
BA-BAAAM

00:13:55.210 --> 00:13:57.330
All of the baths run from
a hot spring source,

00:13:57.330 --> 00:14:00.170
but we're going to take a dip
in the hot spring itself.

00:14:00.550 --> 00:14:02.760
Want to come with, Kiriyama?

00:14:04.550 --> 00:14:07.220
Also, this. The program for tonight's reception.

00:14:07.550 --> 00:14:09.300
Take a glance at it.

00:14:09.430 --> 00:14:11.560
Well, let's meet in the lobby at 6:00.

00:14:13.060 --> 00:14:15.560
UMINO EGG

00:14:15.560 --> 00:14:21.070
ALONE...

00:14:23.070 --> 00:14:27.070
GLANCE
GLANCE

00:14:23.490 --> 00:14:27.070
The room is so spacious, fancy, and quiet that he can't relax...

00:14:30.240 --> 00:14:33.330
<i>Hot spring... hot spring?</i>

00:14:33.950 --> 00:14:36.250
<i>A hot spring, huh?</i>

00:14:38.290 --> 00:14:42.630
<i>Come to think of it,
I guess I've never been in one.</i>

00:14:45.720 --> 00:14:47.550
SILENCE...

00:14:51.050 --> 00:14:53.470
Doesn't have the courage
to go to the bigger baths
with everyone...

00:14:51.050 --> 00:14:53.470
Modern Kid...
(Has never been
in a bath with
someone else...)

00:14:54.100 --> 00:14:56.230
Um, the program...

00:14:57.940 --> 00:15:00.400
First, the chairman greets everyone.

00:15:00.400 --> 00:15:05.610
Then the flower presentation,
guests' address, sponsor speeches,

00:15:05.610 --> 00:15:08.990
a toast from the president
of the sponsoring newspaper...

00:15:09.320 --> 00:15:09.990
Huh?

00:15:10.570 --> 00:15:14.410
Players' address, Q&A session with the players,

00:15:14.580 --> 00:15:18.750
photo session with the players,
players' signing...

00:15:29.340 --> 00:15:32.010
<i>The reception that night was a lavish affair,</i>

00:15:32.010 --> 00:15:33.760
Welcome Newcomer Tournament
Commemorative Match Reception
Meijin Touji Souya and Rei Kiriyama 5th-Dan

00:15:34.760 --> 00:15:36.270
<i>overflowing with people,</i>

00:15:40.600 --> 00:15:42.560
<i>with lots of flash bulbs going off,</i>

00:15:44.150 --> 00:15:46.530
<i>and lots of speeches being made.</i>

00:15:51.870 --> 00:15:57.950
<i>I see. It takes a lot of stamina and will power
to make it through these things.</i>

00:15:58.500 --> 00:16:02.580
<i>I've been bowing so much that I feel dizzy.</i>

00:16:04.540 --> 00:16:07.550
<i>I can't think of anything to say.</i>

00:16:13.430 --> 00:16:16.390
<i>Is this kind of thing run-of-the-mill for him?</i>

00:16:17.390 --> 00:16:21.900
<i>Has he been standing alone
in this world all this time?</i>

00:16:24.810 --> 00:16:27.480
<i>When he's surrounded
by all of these unfamiliar people</i>

00:16:27.480 --> 00:16:31.860
<i>and steeling himself, I want to support him
so he's not worn out before the first match.</i>

00:16:32.530 --> 00:16:33.780
<i>Nikaidou...</i>

00:16:34.280 --> 00:16:39.200
<i>You always had an idea
of what was going on.</i>

00:16:40.750 --> 00:16:42.000
<i>More than me.</i>

00:16:46.380 --> 00:16:48.550
<i>Don't try to act cool, Kiriyama!</i>

00:16:48.550 --> 00:16:50.920
<i>If you really want to win, then persevere!</i>

00:16:50.920 --> 00:16:55.100
<i>Take better care of your shogi,
and yourself!</i>

00:17:04.060 --> 00:17:06.020
<i>If he hadn't said that to me,</i>

00:17:06.360 --> 00:17:08.940
<i>I'm sure I wouldn't be standing here right now.</i>

00:17:11.110 --> 00:17:12.820
<i>And next to him.</i>

00:17:27.540 --> 00:17:31.630
<i>I wanted to find out
what was on the other side of the storm,</i>

00:17:32.550 --> 00:17:36.090
<i>but I realized how unprepared I was</i>

00:17:36.430 --> 00:17:40.600
<i>to ask that question when I saw his profile.</i>

00:17:47.060 --> 00:17:49.070
<i>And I also realized</i>

00:17:50.480 --> 00:17:53.900
<i>that I had never even
entered a storm before.</i>

00:17:55.740 --> 00:17:58.320
This is your first match
with Meijin Souya, isn't it?

00:17:58.320 --> 00:18:01.450
How do you feel?
What kind of battle would you like to have?

00:18:03.540 --> 00:18:04.580
Um...

00:18:05.250 --> 00:18:08.960
<i>The expressions "it's an honor"
and "I'll return blow for blow"</i>

00:18:08.960 --> 00:18:16.890
<i>popped into my head, but what I understood
was not that, so I couldn't speak properly.</i>

00:18:18.090 --> 00:18:20.720
<i>It would take playing against him
several times</i>

00:18:20.720 --> 00:18:23.560
<i>before I could get a sense
of the distance between us.</i>

00:18:24.270 --> 00:18:26.100
<i>That's how far away he was.</i>

00:18:28.230 --> 00:18:34.610
I-I want to concentrate as I play
so the match isn't over as soon as it's begun.

00:18:35.110 --> 00:18:37.030
The next question is for Meijin Souya.

00:18:37.030 --> 00:18:39.870
Could you say a few words
about Kiriyama 5th-Dan?

00:18:40.280 --> 00:18:42.950
I saw his game records
from the Newcomer Tournament,

00:18:42.950 --> 00:18:46.160
and I could tell he's really studying hard.

00:18:46.160 --> 00:18:49.380
I like how even so,
he has a flexible playing style.

00:18:51.920 --> 00:18:54.630
How do you think the match will go tomorrow?

00:18:56.050 --> 00:19:00.890
This will be our first match together, so I'd like
to see what kind of flow we can create.

00:19:01.220 --> 00:19:03.390
<i>H-He's so good at this.</i>

00:19:03.390 --> 00:19:05.020
Ah, yes, yes.

00:19:03.810 --> 00:19:14.400
GLOW...

00:19:05.020 --> 00:19:08.480
Well said, Meijin Souya.
You've got a way with words.

00:19:08.810 --> 00:19:12.690
Meijin Souya, you've been participating
in championship matches all year,

00:19:12.690 --> 00:19:14.400
so how are you holding up physically?

00:19:14.780 --> 00:19:18.910
I've been coming to Iwate
for a number of championship matches,

00:19:19.320 --> 00:19:22.410
but I'd also like to visit someday
without playing a match.

00:19:25.450 --> 00:19:30.170
<i>M-Meijin Souya. Could he be out of it?</i>

00:19:31.500 --> 00:19:34.880
I don't think that answer
really matches the question...

00:19:36.130 --> 00:19:39.430
U-Um... Okay, one more.

00:19:39.760 --> 00:19:42.260
All right, thank you.

00:19:42.720 --> 00:19:43.680
Excuse me.

00:19:50.190 --> 00:19:51.480
I-I'm sorry!

00:19:51.650 --> 00:19:53.190
Oh no! Your suit!

00:19:53.190 --> 00:19:55.110
Meijin Souya, are you all right?

00:19:58.950 --> 00:20:02.700
Mr. Souya, um, your clothes...

00:20:03.200 --> 00:20:08.870
Yes. I believe many people from here
in Morioka will come tomorrow,

00:20:09.160 --> 00:20:11.040
so I would like to do my best

00:20:11.040 --> 00:20:16.500
to have a great match with Kiriyama 5th-Dan
that everyone will enjoy.

00:20:21.590 --> 00:20:24.470
<i>Everyone who was there held their breath.</i>

00:20:25.890 --> 00:20:31.440
<i>No matter how different someone is,
if they're strong, your path is justified.</i>

00:20:32.900 --> 00:20:35.110
Oh, what are you doing, Souya?

00:20:35.650 --> 00:20:37.860
What? Drenched in red wine?

00:20:37.860 --> 00:20:40.110
I take my eyes off of you
for one minute and this happens!

00:20:40.110 --> 00:20:41.360
You absent-minded general!

00:20:41.700 --> 00:20:43.780
Come with me! You need to get that off!

00:20:43.780 --> 00:20:45.950
What are you going to do
for the match tomorrow?

00:20:45.950 --> 00:20:49.660
That's the only suit you brought, right? Sheesh!

00:20:51.330 --> 00:20:53.210
Red wine?

00:20:54.500 --> 00:20:59.050
I'll do what I can with the stain right away,
but I don't know if it'll come out.

00:20:59.590 --> 00:21:02.220
Souya, it's on your shirt and tie too!

00:21:05.760 --> 00:21:10.730
<i>After he left, everyone let out their held breath.</i>

00:21:11.430 --> 00:21:14.230
<i>And then someone muttered a few words.</i>

00:21:14.940 --> 00:21:17.650
That's a shogi demon.

00:21:17.770 --> 00:21:21.490
He's barely holding on to his human form.

00:21:26.740 --> 00:21:29.990
<i>Then, the morning of the match came.</i>

00:21:35.330 --> 00:21:36.500
Meijin Souya!

00:21:36.500 --> 00:21:38.000
Huh? Traditional Japanese clothes...

00:22:34.680 --> 00:22:36.270
<i>That morning,</i>

00:22:37.560 --> 00:22:39.810
<i>an unseasonable typhoon</i>

00:22:39.810 --> 00:22:42.860
<i>went from the sea around Amami Ooshima
and made landfall in Kagoshima.</i>

00:22:44.280 --> 00:22:45.320
<i>And then</i>

00:22:46.820 --> 00:22:49.120
<i>the news said that the typhoon</i>

00:22:49.620 --> 00:22:55.580
<i>was slowly moving north, as if it was
licking the Japanese archipelago.</i>

00:22:57.540 --> 00:23:00.040
White Storm (Part 1)

00:24:30.010 --> 00:24:32.010
Next Episode Preview

00:24:32.010 --> 00:24:38.680
Episode 37

00:24:33.470 --> 00:24:35.180
He reminds me of a bird.

00:24:36.310 --> 00:24:41.100
Starting right now,
I have to cross paths with him.

00:24:42.600 --> 00:24:46.610
This white bird with huge wings...

00:24:47.780 --> 00:24:49.030
Let's have a good game.

00:24:50.030 --> 00:24:59.040
ILLUSTRATION:
TETSUO HARA

00:24:50.990 --> 00:24:54.700
Toku, I'll take another picture
you can use for a poster,

00:24:54.700 --> 00:24:57.370
so next time
make me look cool, okay?
